  "name": "auditing-third-party-plugins",
  "description": "Security principles and the shared audit procedure for third-party plugins, extensions and packages that run code inside an agent, editor, terminal or IDE: pinning, execution freeze, full source review, effective versus declared authority, update deltas and verdicts. Use before installing, enabling, linking, building or updating any third-party plugin, when asked whether a plugin is safe, and when a plugin platform offers auto-updates. Ecosystem skills such as managing-pi-packages, managing-herdr-plugins and managing-orca-plugins hold each platform's commands and load this one.",
